SharedLvmThin for Proxmox VE
============================

EXPERIMENTAL TEST SOFTWARE -- DISPOSABLE LABS ONLY
--------------------------------------------------

Both Thin mode and Thick Generations mode are experimental. Neither mode is
production-ready, supported, certified, or warranted. Use only disposable
hosts, disposable shared storage, and disposable guest data. Use can cause
data loss, corruption, unavailability, failed migration or recovery, and host
or cluster downtime. The operator is responsible for fencing, independent
tested backups, recovery, SAN identity, multipath behavior, capacity, change
control, and all use decisions.

No support, maintenance, response time, service level, update schedule,
compatibility commitment, or duty to fix is offered. See the repository's
README.md and docs/RISK-AND-SUPPORT-BOUNDARY.md before use. GNU GPLv3 sections
15 through 17 contain the warranty disclaimer and limitation of liability.

Components
----------

SharedLvmThinPlugin.pm
    Proxmox VE shared LVM thin storage backend.

pve-sharedlvmthin-monitor
    dmeventd thin-pool monitoring and cluster-safe autogrow helper.

sharedlvmthin
    Health, compatibility and deep validation CLI.

sharedlvmthin-health-json
    Read-only machine-readable health collector.

sharedlvmthin-web
    Optional read-only HTTPS health dashboard.

sharedlvmthin-web-configure
    Interactive dashboard network, TLS and access configuration.


Health Check
------------

    sharedlvmthin doctor


Deep Validation
---------------

Deep validation performs temporary write operations and must only be
started explicitly by an administrator from the CLI against disposable data.

    sharedlvmthin doctor --deep

Deep validation is intentionally not exposed as a web action.


Web Dashboard
-------------

Configure or reconfigure:

    sharedlvmthin-web-configure

The dashboard:

- uses HTTPS
- binds only to the selected host IP
- delegates authentication to Proxmox VE
- does not store PVE passwords
- requires an authenticated administrator
- exposes health information read-only
- does not expose storage write operations

The storage plugin does not depend on the web dashboard. Failure or
disablement of the web service does not affect the storage data path.
